From c052a286eb832a82cb8825be16ffd820dda873c3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Deniz Kokden <koekdendeniz@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 22:48:55 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 028/110] pwm: add a driver for the Spreadtrum SC8830/SC7730
 PWM

The always-on PWM block of the SC8830 family has four channels with an
8-bit prescaler and an 8-bit counter: duty and modulus share one
register, the enable bit sits in the prescaler register, and two
pattern registers must read all ones. Mainline pwm-sprd covers the
later UMS512 block, whose layout differs. Duty 0 stops the counter
like the vendor's backlight-off state. Until the SoC has a clock driver
the driver opens its channel gate and selects the 26 MHz source.

Takes over the bootloader state (Galaxy Tab E backlight, duty 143 of
255 at 20.4 kHz) without a glitch.

Assisted-by: Claude Opus 5.5
Signed-off-by: Deniz Kokden <koekdendeniz@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/pwm/Kconfig           |  12 +++
 drivers/pwm/Makefile          |   1 +
 drivers/pwm/pwm-sprd-sc8830.c | 184 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 3 files changed, 197 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 drivers/pwm/pwm-sprd-sc8830.c

